 "_doc": "The eight lanes Prabhat can actually reach, derived from the 78 tailored variants in cv/variants/. Each lane lists the search phrases fired at every source. Keep phrases as an employer would title the job, never as a level ('junior', 'debutant' produce student contracts: harvest_rules.md). Entry-level phrases ('junior buyer', 'supply chain junior', 'junior pricing analyst') were added 2026-11-02 for procurement, supply chain, planning and pricing: stage, alternance and VIE titles are still rejected by rules.json, so 'junior' no longer pulls student contracts. Prabh, 2026-11-02: 'very less ops are coming for supply chain, buyer, junior buyer, procurement analysis, pricing - we should be targetting all kind of entry roles too'.",
